@@ -66,6 +66,27 @@ diff -Naur busybox-1.36.1.ori/networking
 ```
 
 ## Configuration
+### Video parameters
+
+Each profile accepts `bitrate` (kbps), `framerate` (numerator),
+`framerate_den` (default 1), `gov_length`, `encoding_interval`, `quality`
+and `encoding_profile` (for example `Baseline`, `Main` or `High`). Text and
+JSON configurations use the same field names. Profile names must be unique.
+Set these fields to the actual encoder configuration. Compatibility defaults
+are 30 fps, GOP 40, quality 100, encoding interval 1 and H264 High/H265 Main.
+A bitrate of zero denotes an unspecified limit; no bandwidth is invented.
+
+Media2 reports fractional frame rates. Media1 requires an integer upper
+frame-rate limit, so a fractional rate is rounded upwards for that field.
+H265 streams are exposed through Media2 and excluded from Media1. JPEG
+descriptions omit inter-frame codec settings. Static configuration options
+describe current settings.
+
+Optional global `source_width`, `source_height`, `source_framerate` and
+`source_framerate_den` describe the sensor independently of encoded outputs.
+Without source dimensions, the largest configured output provides the legacy
+fallback. The source token remains stable when profiles change.
+
 Set `ONVIF_LOG_FILE=-` in the CGI environment to log to stderr. A pathname
 selects an append-only log managed by the HTTP host. With the variable unset,
 the existing log file and rotation behaviour are retained.
